<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11662" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπᾰφίσκω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cheat, beguile,</i> mostly in compos. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρά</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ</span>:— of the simple word <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> has only 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαφίσκει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.217
				</span></i>
			: aor. opt. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπάφοιτο</span> in act. sense, <i><span class="en">
				23.216
			</span></i>:—later, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπάφῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>APl.</u>
					4.108
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Jul.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαφών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					3.444
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤπαφες, ἤπαφε,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				3.49
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				5.512
			</span></i>: aor. 1
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπάφησε</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				8.129
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				13.280
			</span></i>, 2sg.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπάφησας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.502
				</span></i>
			.</div>
